url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21782008"
abstract: >-
  The tensor-product and commuting-operator suprema of the canonical I3322
  Bell functional are identified with a rigorously characterized domain-wall
  constant. A normal spatial strategy attains the value, while no
  finite-dimensional strategy does. Consequently C_q(3,3;2,2) differs from
  C_qs(3,3;2,2), and the scenario is minimal by bipartite binary input counts.
keywords:
